class:: BlipWidth
summary:: Finite bandlimited pulse with independent width and harmonic count
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDiff, Classes/BlipDisp, Classes/BlipFB, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipKernel, Classes/BlipPM, Classes/BlipPeak, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipSeries

description::

BlipWidth reconstructs a bipolar periodic rectangle whose harmonic
coefficients follow code::sin(pi * k * width) / (pi * k)::. Harmonic count is
explicit and independent of width.

The implementation is informed by the two-edge BLIT structure of
link::Classes/Pulse:: but does not inherit its free-running leaky integrator.
It integrates closed-form derivatives with respect to phase and width,
maintains separate old/new states during topology changes, and re-anchors to
the exact finite series at phase wraps. Per-sample cost is constant; the
occasional O(N) re-anchor has a bounded average cost under harmonic limiting.

The zero-mean finite series is scaled by code::2 * max(width, 1 - width):: so
its wider plateau is approximately one. Finite-series Gibbs overshoot remains
possible. Width is clipped to a small open interval, negative frequency is
supported, and zero frequency holds phase while width changes remain audible.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Pulse::. Pulse chooses bandwidth
automatically; BlipWidth exposes the finite harmonic count and uses
drift-resistant re-anchoring.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numharm
Requested harmonic count, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..2048::
before Nyquist limiting.

argument:: width
Audio- or control-rate duty ratio. Values are clipped close to, but not at,
zero and one.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier; it is outside the integrator state.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset; it is outside the integrator state.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipWidth.ar(100, 40, 0.5, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipWidth.ar(80, 60, SinOsc.ar(0.1).range(0.02, 0.8), 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipWidth.ar(SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(50, 400), LFNoise1.kr(0.5).range(1, 100), LFNoise1.kr(1).range(0.1, 0.9)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
